    "chunk_text": "IV ^wd& jeks fldgi \u2013 YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'06'03Part IV (B) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 03.06.20191A\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2137$4 - 2019 wf.daia;= ui 19 jeks i\u00f7od - 2019'08'19No. 2137/4 - MONDAY AUGUST 19, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nFILLING OF A VACANCY IN THE OFFICE OF MEMBER OF THE PUTTALAM URBANCOUNCIL UNDER SECTION 66A(1) OF THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES ELECTIONS ORDINANCE(CHAPTER 262)\n\nWHEREAS the office of return member of Puttalam Urban Council has fallen vacant by reason of Resignation ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Secretary of the National Front For Good Governance, the recognized political party towhich Mohamad Thaha Noorul Ameen the member belonged, was required by me under Section 66 A (1) of the aforesaidordinance, to decide upon returned member of Puttalam Urban Council who belongs to such party and is not disqualifiedunder Section 9 of the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance and who shall be declared selected as a member within aperiod of thirty (30) days ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Secretary of the aforesaid recognized Political Party has communicated his decision tonominate Ahamed Kabeer Siththi Saleema to fill such vacancy ;\n\nNOW THEREFORE, I, Nagalingam Regan, Returning Officer of the Puttalam Urban Council, acting in terms ofSection 66A(1) of the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance (Chapter 262) do hereby declare that Ahamed KabeerSiththi Saleema was selected as the member of the Puttalam Urban Council.\n\nN. REGAN,Returning Officer,Puttalam Urban Council.District Election Office,Puttalam,16th August, 2019.\n\n09 - 06\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART IV (B) \u2014 LOCAL GOVERNMENT\n\nNotices under the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk1A - G 30740\u2014 27 (08/2019)PRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
